{"parentUuid":"7c0a9290-c3e3-4817-8fa2-0500c8411952","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"edac4314-7853-44b7-9152-71a2296efc96","agentId":"a9ad0a3f3c5057347","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fia5zmgMo1eqog7aUoZ6ad","type":"tool_result","content":"=== keystone-unified-snapshot.js ===\n      98 /Users/kristinarash/.claude/hooks/keystone-unified-snapshot.js\n      31 /Users/kristinarash/.codex/hooks/keystone-unified-snapshot.js\n     129 total\n--- diff line count ---\n     109\n--- first 15 diff lines ---\n2,14c2,5\n< // SessionStart hook: inject the Tier B global memory snapshot (USER.md,\n< // MEMORY.md, and .errors.log when non-empty) plus KeystoneOS's cross-harness\n< // unified snapshot, alongside the memory compiler's own snapshot.\n< //\n< // This replaces the prose instruction in ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md that told the\n< // agent to read those three files by hand at session start — a rule nothing\n< // enforced, which therefore silently did not happen in some sessions.\n< //\n< // Fails closed: any error means less context, never a thrown error that could\n< // block session start. But a MISSING SOURCE IS REPORTED, not swallowed — the\n< // old version pointed at the retired ~/Desktop/DEV path and injected nothing\n< // at all for weeks without a single visible symptom (see project memory\n< // `memsearch-index-path-drift`: make fallbacks loud).\n---\n\n=== memsearch-sync.js.bak-2026-09-02 ===\n     210 /Users/kristinarash/.claude/hooks/memsearch-sync.js.bak-2026-09-02\n     191 /Users/kristinarash/.codex/hooks/memsearch-sync.js.bak-2026-09-02\n     401 total\n--- diff line count ---\n      75\n--- first 15 diff lines ---\n26,43c26,30\n< // Declared before resolvePaths() runs: `const PATHS = resolvePaths()` executes\n< // below, and resolvePaths now calls logErr on the fallback branch. If ERR_LOG\n< // were still declared further down it would be in the temporal dead zone at\n< // that moment, and logErr's own try/catch would swallow the ReferenceError —\n< // turning the loud fallback warning silent again.\n< const ERR_LOG = path.join(os.homedir(), '.claude', 'global-memory', 'transcripts', '.errors.log');\n< \n< function logErr(msg) {\n<   try { fs.appendFileSync(ERR_LOG, `[${new Date().toISOString()}] memsearch-sync: ${msg}\\n`); }\n<   catch (_) {}\n< }\n< \n< // Single source of truth, shared with daily-backup.ps1 and the Codex hook.\n< // Was ~/Desktop/DEV on Windows; DEV lives at ~/DEV on the Mac. The stale path\n\n=== transcript-capture.js ===\n     110 /Users/kristinarash/.claude/hooks/transcript-capture.js\n     110 /Users/kristinarash/.codex/hooks/transcript-capture.js\n     220 total\n--- diff line count ---\n      10\n--- first 15 diff lines ---\n71,74c71,74\n<   // A null/absent transcript_path is not breakage — some harnesses that share\n<   // these hooks (Codex `gpt-5.6*` sessions, verified 2026-09-07) never supply\n<   // one. There is nothing to capture, so exit quietly. Logging it refilled\n<   // .errors.log every run and buried the entries that do mean something.\n---\n>   // A null/absent transcript_path is not breakage — Codex `gpt-5.6*` sessions\n>   // never supply one (verified 2026-09-07). There is nothing to capture, so\n>   // exit quietly. Logging it refilled .errors.log every run and buried the\n>   // entries that do mean something.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"51c08195-5750-49f9-a5de-38b995f3e9c6","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:30:12.167Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== keystone-unified-snapshot.js ===\n      98 /Users/kristinarash/.claude/hooks/keystone-unified-snapshot.js\n      31 /Users/kristinarash/.codex/hooks/keystone-unified-snapshot.js\n     129 total\n--- diff line count ---\n     109\n--- first 15 diff lines ---\n2,14c2,5\n< // SessionStart hook: inject the Tier B global memory snapshot (USER.md,\n< // MEMORY.md, and .errors.log when non-empty) plus KeystoneOS's cross-harness\n< // unified snapshot, alongside the memory compiler's own snapshot.\n< //\