{"parentUuid":"c4ee02ac-7304-4a7f-903c-18cc08cdc372","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a9ad0a3f3c5057347","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CezyA12PTJ1edBzaK8Jpn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Findings\n\n**RED — Codex `keystone-unified-snapshot.js` is a stale/reverted copy.** `~/.claude/hooks/keystone-unified-snapshot.js` (98 lines) injects USER.md, MEMORY.md, `.errors.log` (when non-empty), and a KeystoneOS pointer, with loud-failure handling for missing required sources. `~/.codex/hooks/keystone-unified-snapshot.js` (31 lines) is the old pre-revision version — it injects only the bare KeystoneOS snapshot and has none of the USER.md/MEMORY.md/error-surfacing logic. Codex sessions are silently running without the user-profile/memory injection your CLAUDE.md describes as universal. This is a live recurrence of the known \"hook two-copies trap\" (project memory). Fix: copy the current `.claude/hooks` version over the `.codex/hooks` copy.\n\n**AMBER — `transcript-capture.js` differs only in comment wording** (10-line diff, all inside a comment block explaining the null-transcript-path skip); logic is otherwise identical. No functional drift; no action needed beyond noting it for the memory-file drift ledger.\n\n**AMBER — `memsearch-sync.js.bak-2026-09-02` differs** (75-line diff, mostly comments/log-path documentation). It's a `.bak-*` file, not a live hook in either directory, so it isn't executing — low stakes, but worth pruning since dead backups are exactly what causes future confusion about \"which copy is canonical.\"\n\n**AMBER — stale compile lock self-healed.** `.errors.log` (1 line) shows `compiler-stale-lock: reclaimed compile lock held 1550min by pid 47899` at 2026-09-13 04:30 UTC — `compile.py --auto` was stuck for ~25.8 hours before the lock was reclaimed. `compile.log` shows it then successfully compiled 2026-09-11 and 2026-09-12 (8 and 6 articles written, KB now 272 articles). Resolved, but a stuck compile process going undetected for a full day is worth a closer look at what killed/hung pid 47899.\n\n**GREEN — launchd agents.** All `com.keystone.*` jobs loaded, last exit code 0 (`commandcentre` shows PID 1047 running); no jobs in a failed state.\n\n**GREEN — venv/memsearch.** `claude-memory-compiler/.venv` resolves to a live `cpython-3.12-macos-aarch64` interpreter (3.12.13). `memsearch` binary resolves via the uv-tool symlink and reports v0.4.17 successfully.\n\n**GREEN — flush pipeline.** No stranded `session-flush-*.md` files in `scripts/`; `flush.log` tail shows normal `SessionEnd fired` → `Flush complete` cycles through 2026-09-12 23:30, including expected `SKIP: no transcript path`/`transcript missing` for job-trigger and empty-context sessions (benign, documented pattern). Daily logs present through 2026-09-12.\n\n**GREEN — backup freshness.** Last `daily-backup.log` run: 2026-09-12 14:28:19, ended `OK (0 errors)`, with `RECEIPT ssd : verified run=20260912-142439` — the CRASHBOX SSD was mounted and captured for that run (earlier runs same day logged `NOT MOUNTED — SKIPPED`, but the final run got a real receipt). Current time is pre-09:00 on 2026-09-13, so today's scheduled run hasn't fired yet — not stale.\n\n**GREEN — cross-machine handoff.** `global-memory` is 0 ahead / 0 behind `origin/main` (only uncommitted local working-tree changes from tonight, normal pre-commit state).\n\n## Hook name diff (`.claude/hooks` vs `.codex/hooks`)\n\n- Only in `~/.claude/hooks` (2): `herdr-agent-state.sh`, `memsearch-sync.js.bak-20260814` — both look intentional/inert (a `.bak` snapshot and what appears to be a Claude-only agent-state helper), not drift by omission.\n- Only in `~/.codex/hooks`: none.\n- Present in both, contents differ (3): `keystone-unified-snapshot.js` (substantive — RED, see above), `memsearch-sync.js.bak-2026-09-02` (comment-only, dead file), `transcript-capture.js` (comment-only, no logic change).\n- Counts matched expectations: 61 in `.claude/hooks`, 59 in `.codex/hooks`.\n\n## Checked\nRead `SKILL.md`; listed/diffed hook filenames (`ls`, `diff`, `comm`); `shasum -a 256` + `diff` on all 59 shared hook files; `launchctl list | grep keystone`; venv symlink + `--version`; `memsearch --version`; `.errors.log`, `flush.log`, `compile.log`, `last-flush.json` location; `daily-backup.log` tail and CRASHBOX receipt lines; `/Volumes` mount state; `git status`/`rev-list` on `~/.claude/global-memory` and `~/.claude`.\n\n## Not checked\nDid not run `stack-check.ps1`/`handoff-check.ps1` themselves (avoided invoking pwsh scripts under a strict no-mutation mandate even though documented read-only, to stay conservative); did not check `com.keystone.morning`/`rituals`/`adjudicate` job *content* beyond exit code; did not verify MCP/plugin auth rot (out of this skill's scope per its own doc); did not inspect Windows-side state (no access from this session)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1174,"cache_read_input_tokens":77964,"output_tokens":2402,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":468},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1174},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2402,"cache_read_input_tokens":77964,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1174,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1174,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cezy9zeJuGX8MusVHUn9N","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionSkill":"update-config","type":"assistant","uuid":"8378c23c-30d2-4c1c-8550-8e885b734c37","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:31:41.608Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKi